 The [dialogue study](TARANTINO_CASE_STUDY.md) develops the craft of an encounter through Tarantino’s own accounts of writing and revising. Give the speakers room to pursue their immediate concerns. bob can want to hear a new roller; ed can want to know how much space to leave in a register. The listener’s response tells us whether they share the interest, tolerate it or intend to put it to use. Avoid making every worker equally quick, articulate or amusing. A plain answer can carry the greatest cost in the room.
 
+Owner dialogue direction · 22 October 2026 (`owner-dialogue-quality-1792682200`): pursue a practical agenda with a real listener. Let status change through a request, a refusal, an evasion or a small detail somebody will not let go. A tangent must reveal its speaker or prepare a payoff. Leave short answers and silence where pressure makes them useful. Keep the scene short enough to play.
+
+Use original Loopforge language. Reject generic robot banter, forced mechanical puns, canned swagger, ornamental profanity and speeches that announce a theme or diagnose a character. Tarantino’s dialogue is a craft reference; never copy or closely paraphrase film lines. Judge the exchange before its author’s rationale. Mark silent rhythm review as text-only; a correct transcript does not establish a good performance.
+
 Draft the conversation before dividing it into bubbles. Read it aloud through every part, including the listener who is working, waiting or trying to leave. Revise once from the position of the person with least power to end it. Then fit words, gestures, pauses and object handling together. A line may change a belief, but that consequence belongs to whoever heard and understood it; the scene must not distribute knowledge or reconciliation to everyone because a sentence was spoken.
 
 For a short staged introduction, keep the exchange that changes the room and cut the explanation around it. Routine checks can happen under an order or a reply. Do not use long pauses to lend weight to every sentence. Save time for a revealing action, a reversal, or an answer the speaker finds difficult. Test the performed cut at normal playback speed: good prose on a page can still be dead time on screen.
